        "id": 87610,
        "name": "Matchstickman",
        "username": "Matchstickman",
        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/matchstickman/{size}/1880_2.png",
        "created_at": "2014-02-04T22:57:13.000Z",
        "cooked": "<aside class=\"quote group-playtesters\" data-username=\"Silverleaf\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n<img loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/silverleaf/48/2332_2.png\" class=\"avatar\"> Silverleaf:</div>\n<blockquote>\n<p>I find that the best \"screw you\" games are the ones that look very innocent.</p>\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p>I find the best screw you games are the ones that say \"Hey, you need to screw your buddy to win but if you screw them too much then I, the game, win!\"</p>\n<p>Cutthroat Caverns is a nice example of that, and has a familar RPG-esk theme.</p>",
